Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(autoFarmer): hadResearch is truthful on the
 sellability-skip path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One token: `hadResearch: true` becomes `hadResearch: !!research` on the
skip_low_demand / skip_probe_budget record() call in processCampaign. Every
other record() call in that function already writes `!!research`; this one
hardcoded true, so an unscanned game that skipped (probing refused by the
cold-start cooldown or budget) was recorded as having had market research
when it had none. Found while building the replay harness
(FARM2-VERIFICATION §5.1). Own commit so it can be deployed or held on its own.

What reads hadResearch — as far as this checkout can show: nothing. It is
written on 13 sites (autoFarmer.js x10, farm2 decide/execute x3) and declared
on the AutoFarmTask model. No route, page, auto-lister, Telegram message,
allocation forecast or farm2 step reads it; the replay harness selects it in a
projection and never uses it (it branches on the decision instead, precisely
because this field could not be trusted). grep -rn hadResearch, excluding
node_modules, finds only writers, the model, tests and docs.

What this checkout cannot show: production runs 79 lines of autoFarmer.js and
17 of autoLister.js this tree does not have, plus utils/catalogPreorder.js,
which exists only there. Any of those could read the field. I have no way to
check from a sandbox, so: harmless as far as the visible code goes, and
holdable if prod-only code turns out to depend on the old value.

Three tests drive the real processCampaign: an unscanned game inside the probe
cooldown skips and now records hadResearch false; a researched skip still
records true; the host-gate path, always truthful, is the control. Suite
694/695 vs 691/692 after the previous commit; the single failure is unchanged.
